{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Python code to GNU C++11 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Python 3 code to GNU C++11 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Python 3 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n<your_rewritten_code_2>\nimport itertools\nimport bisect\n\nn, m = map(int, input().split())\na = list(map(int, input().split()))\n\ndef get_modular_sums(arr, mod):\n    res = []\n    for r in range(len(arr)+1):\n        for comb in itertools.combinations(arr, r):\n            res.append(sum(comb) % mod)\n    return res\n\nn1 = n // 2\na1_mods = get_modular_sums(a[:n1], m)\na2_mods = get_modular_sums(a[n1:], m)\n\na1_unique_sorted = sorted(set(a1_mods))\n\ndef find_best_pair(x):\n    target = m - x\n    idx = bisect.bisect_left(a1_unique_sorted, target)\n    if idx == 0:\n        return x\n    return a1_unique_sorted[idx-1] + x\n\nresults = [find_best_pair(val) for val in a2_mods]\nprint(max(results))\n</your_rewritten_code_2>\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <set>\n#include <cmath>\n#include <climits>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nvector<int> get_modular_sums(const vector<int>& arr, int mod) {\n    vector<int> res;\n    int n = arr.size();\n    // Iterate through all possible subsets (2^n subsets)\n    for (int mask = 0; mask < (1 << n); mask++) {\n        int sum = 0;\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            if (mask & (1 << i)) {\n                sum += arr[i];\n            }\n        }\n        res.push_back(sum % mod);\n    }\n    return res;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int n, m;\n    cin >> n >> m;\n    \n    vector<int> a(n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        cin >> a[i];\n    }\n    \n    int n1 = n / 2;\n    vector<int> a1(a.begin(), a.begin() + n1);\n    vector<int> a2(a.begin() + n1, a.end());\n    \n    vector<int> a1_mods = get_modular_sums(a1, m);\n    vector<int> a2_mods = get_modular_sums(a2, m);\n    \n    set<int> a1_unique_set(a1_mods.begin(), a1_mods.end());\n    vector<int> a1_unique_sorted(a1_unique_set.begin(), a1_unique_set.end());\n    sort(a1_unique_sorted.begin(), a1_unique_sorted.end());\n    \n    vector<int> results;\n    for (int val : a2_mods) {\n        int target = m - val;\n        // Find the largest element in a1_unique_sorted that is <= target-1\n        int idx = lower_bound(a1_unique_sorted.begin(), a1_unique_sorted.end(), target) - a1_unique_sorted.begin();\n        int best;\n        if (idx == 0) {\n            best = val;\n        } else {\n            best = a1_unique_sorted[idx - 1] + val;\n        }\n        results.push_back(best);\n    }\n    \n    int max_result = 0;\n    for (int res : results) {\n        if (res > max_result) {\n            max_result = res;\n        }\n    }\n    cout << max_result << endl;\n    \n    return 0;\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00016199229867197573, -2.622600959512056e-06, -5.960462772236497e-07, -0.0002227773511549458, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -9.262132516596466e-05, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -3.814689989667386e-06, -1.0728830375228426e-06, -1.5258672647178173e-05, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -1.31130127556